  "instructions": [
    "Toss the pork with the salt, pepper, cumin, and oregano in a large bowl. Let it sit while you prep the rest.",
    "Set a 6 quart electric pressure cooker to saute on high. Add the olive oil and heat for 2 minutes.",
    "Brown the pork in two batches, about 3 minutes per side, until deeply golden. Move each batch to a plate.",
    "Pour the orange juice and lime juice into the pot. Scrape up the browned bits from the bottom.",
    "Return the pork to the pot. Add the yellow onion wedges and garlic.",
    "Lock the lid and seal the vent. Cook on high pressure for 40 minutes, then let the pressure release naturally for 10 minutes before opening the vent.",
    "Heat the oven broiler to high. Shred the pork with two forks. It should fall apart with no resistance.",
    "Spread the pork on a rimmed baking sheet and spoon over 1/2 cup of the cooking liquid. Broil 4 to 5 minutes until the edges are browned and crisp.",
    "Warm the tortillas in a dry skillet over medium heat, about 30 seconds per side. Fill with pork, diced white onion, and cilantro.",
    "Cool leftover pork in its juices. Refrigerate up to 4 days or freeze up to 3 months, then reheat in a skillet until steaming hot."
  ],
